"900BU", 5.01, 1.50,"R",15.46,"Applicable in New Jersey:"
"900MU", 5.01,16.96,"R",61.54,"  Any person who knowingly files a statement of claim containing any false or misleading information is subject"
"900MU", 5.88, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"to criminal and civil penalties."
"900BU", 7.51, 1.50,"R",15.87,"Applicable in New Mexico:"
"900MU", 7.51,17.37,"R",61.13,"  Any person who knowingly presents a false or fraudulent claim for payment of a loss or benefit or knowingly"
"900MU", 8.38, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"presents false information in an application for insurance is guilty of a crime and may be subject to civil fines and criminal penalties."
"900BU", 9.91, 1.50,"R",14.28,"Applicable in New York:"
"900MU", 9.91,15.78,"R",62.72,"  Any person who knowingly makes or knowingly assists, abets, solicits or conspires with another to make a false"
"900MU",10.78, 1.50,"R",77.00,"report of the theft, destruction, damage or conversion of any motor vehicle to a law enforcement agency, the department of motor vehicles"
"900MU",11.63, 1.50,"R",77.00,"or an insurance company, commits a fraudulent insurance act, which is a crime, and shall also be subject to a civil penalty not to exceed"
"900MU",12.48, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"five thousand dollars and the value of the subject motor vehicle or stated claim for each violation."
"900BU",14.01, 1.50,"R",11.77,"Applicable in Ohio:"
"900MU",14.01,13.27,"R",65.23,"  Any person who, with intent to defraud or knowing that he is facilitating a fraud against an insurer, submits an"
"900MU",14.88, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"application or files a claim containing a false or deceptive statement is guilty of insurance fraud."
"900BU",16.51, 1.50,"R",14.81,"Applicable in Oklahoma:"
"900MU",16.51,16.31,"R",62.19,"  WARNING: Any person who knowingly, and with intent to injure, defraud or deceive any insurer, makes any"
"900MU",17.38, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"claim for the proceeds of an insurance policy containing any false, incomplete or misleading information is guilty of a felony."
"900BU",19.01, 1.50,"R",13.28,"Applicable in Oregon:"
"900MU",19.01,14.78,"R",63.72," Any person who knowingly and with intent to defraud or solicit another to defraud the insurer by submitting an"
"900MU",19.88, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"application containing a false statement as to any material fact may be violating state law."
"900BU",21.58, 1.50,"R",16.84,"Applicable in Pennsylvania:"
"900MU",21.58,18.34,"R",60.16,"  Any person who knowingly and with intent to injure or defraud any insurer files an application or claim"
"900MU",22.45, 1.50,"R",77.00,"containing any false, incomplete or misleading information shall, upon conviction, be subject to imprisonment for up to seven years and"
"900MU",23.30, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"the payment of a fine of up to $15,000."
"900BU",25.06, 1.50,"R",16.00,"Applicable in Puerto Rico:"
"900MU",25.06,17.50,"R",61.00," Any person who knowingly and with the intention of defrauding presents false information in an insurance"
"900MU",25.93, 1.50,"R",77.00,"application, or presents, helps, or causes the presentation of a fraudulent claim for the payment of a loss or any other benefit, or presents"
"900MU",26.78, 1.50,"R",77.00,"more than one claim for the same damage or loss, shall incur a felony and, upon conviction, shall be sanctioned for each violation by a"
"900MU",27.63, 1.50,"R",77.00,"fine of not less than five thousand dollars ($5,000) and not more than ten thousand dollars ($10,000), or a fixed term of imprisonment for"
"900MU",28.48, 1.50,"R",77.00,"three (3) years, or both penalties. Should aggravating circumstances be present, the penalty thus established may be increased to a"
"900MU",29.33, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"maximum of five (5) years, if extenuating circumstances are present, it may be reduced to a minimum of two (2) years."
"900BU",31.01, 1.50,"R",16.45,"Applicable in Rhode Island:"
"900MU",31.01,17.95,"R",60.55,"  Any person who knowingly presents a false or fraudulent claim for payment of a loss or benefit or knowingly"
"900MU",31.88, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"presents false information in an application for insurance is guilty of a crime and may be subject to fines and confinement in prison."
"900BU",33.51, 1.50,"R",15.10,"Applicable in Tennessee:"
"900MU",33.51,16.60,"R",61.90,"  It is a crime to knowingly provide false, incomplete or misleading information to an insurance company for the"
"900MU",34.38, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"purpose of defrauding the company. Penalties include imprisonment, fines and denial of insurance benefits."
"900BU",36.01, 1.50,"R",12.31,"Applicable in Texas:"
"900MU",36.01,13.81,"R",64.69,"  Any person who knowingly presents a false or fraudulent claim for the payment of a loss is guilty of a crime and"
"900MU",36.88, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"may be subject to fines and confinement in state prison."
"900BU",38.51, 1.50,"R",13.38,"Applicable in Virginia:"
"900MU",38.51,14.88,"R",63.62,"  It is a crime to knowingly provide false, incomplete or misleading information to an insurance company for the"
"900MU",39.38, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"purpose of defrauding the company. Penalties include imprisonment, fines and denial of insurance benefits."
"900BU",41.01, 1.50,"R",15.93,"Applicable in Washington:"
"900MU",41.01,17.42,"R",61.08,"  It is a crime to knowingly provide false, incomplete or misleading information to an insurance company for"
"900MU",41.88, 1.50,"L", 0.00,"the purpose of defrauding the company. Penalties include imprisonment, fines and denial of insurance benefits."
"900BU",43.76, 1.50,"R",16.51,"Applicable in West Virginia:"
"900MU",43.76,18.01,"R",60.49,"  Any person who knowingly presents a false or fraudulent claim for payment of a loss or benefit or knowingly"
